{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensor outcomes from motion commands. The specification binds sensor states to safe, progress-oriented actions: random_walk is used for coverage in clear, safe states; move_forward is used for short, directed progress; rotate_clockwise and rotate_counterclockwise are used for conservative recovery from obstacles; full_rotate is reserved for deadlock or repeated obstacle states. All transitions are deterministic, and uncontrollable events are always handled first. The specification ensures no unsafe forward/random_walk in obstacle states and always returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception (sensors) and motion (actions)",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-biased exploration and conservative obstacle recovery"
  ],
